/T ( In 2018, we transitioned from MATP to the Functional Juggling project, supported by a collaborative and open team of educators and therapists. Stefania initially participated with her right hand tied to her wheelchair \(due to self-injurious behavior and object-mouthing\). She now wears a protective glove and has gained far more freedom and control.)
/E ( In 2018, we transitioned from MATP to the Functional Juggling project, supported by a collaborative and open team of educators and therapists. Stefania initially participated with her right hand tied to her wheelchair \(due to self-injurious behavior and object-mouthing\). She now wears a protective glove and has gained far more freedom and control.)
/Pg 22 0 R
>>
