/E ( Participant Progression: Observable progress was noted across the group. A significant outcome was observed with a non-verbal child with cerebral palsy who had previously shown minimal reaction to external stimuli. Through consistent, one-on-one work with a rolling ball, the child began to participate in a reciprocal back-and-forth interaction by the end of the week. This demonstrated the potential of targeted, patient intervention.)
/Pg 49 0 R
>>
