<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T ( A 9-year-old boy diagnosed with ADHD began attending my circus school in New Jersey, accompanied by his mother, who was seeking support for his struggles with handwriting. Despite being physically capable and cognitively sharp, he found writing frustrating and unengaging. Completing assignments was a battle, and he had developed a strong aversion to the tools themselves. His mother believed his low academic performance was directly tied to his ADHD.)
/E ( A 9-year-old boy diagnosed with ADHD began attending my circus school in New Jersey, accompanied by his mother, who was seeking support for his struggles with handwriting. Despite being physically capable and cognitively sharp, he found writing frustrating and unengaging. Completing assignments was a battle, and he had developed a strong aversion to the tools themselves. His mother believed his low academic performance was directly tied to his ADHD.)
/Pg 58 0 R
>>
